== the two fixes the controller approved for this ticket ==
- lib/source/http_source_transport.dart `withSourceBodyContentType`: okhttp-4.12.0
  `RequestBody$Companion.create(String, MediaType)` parses "<declared>; charset=utf-8"
  when the media type names no charset (bytecode: the literal "; charset=utf-8" is
  appended and re-parsed only when `MediaType.charset()` answers null), so the wire
  carries that value; a declared charset is left untouched.
- `_readOnce` sets `request.contentLength` to the UTF-8 body's byte length before
  writing it, because the frozen client built that body and sends Content-Length.

